    <record id="channel_books_s1_l1" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_books" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Payment reminders</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>Overdue invoices are chased by email on a schedule. <span class="oe-path">Accounting › Configuration › Payment Reminders</span> lists the steps: each has a <strong>Days Offset</strong> from the due date (negative is before it) and the email it sends.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/business_elearning/static/img/reminders.png" alt="Four payment reminder steps from 3 days before due to a final notice" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>the standard schedule: a friendly note 3 days before, on the day, a week late and a final notice.</p></div><p>Reminders go out once a day, each step once per invoice, and stop as soon as it's paid. Edit the emails' wording in <span class="oe-path">Settings › Email Templates</span>. For a customer you'd rather call, tick <strong>Exclude from Automatic Payment Reminders</strong> on their contact.</p></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_books_s1_l2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_books" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">Customer statements</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html"><div class="oe-course-content"><p>A statement lists everything a customer owes. In <span class="oe-path">Accounting › Customers › Customers</span>, tick the customer, then <span class="oe-path">Actions › Partner Outstanding Statement</span>. <strong>View</strong> shows it on screen; <strong>Export PDF</strong> makes one to email.</p><div class="oe-diagram"><img src="/business_elearning/static/img/statement_wizard.png" alt="The outstanding statement options for one customer" class="img-fluid" /><p class="oe-diagram-caption"><span class="oe-diagram-caption-tag">Screenshot</span>an outstanding statement for Bright Path Tutoring.</p></div><p>Tick <strong>Show Aging Buckets</strong> to split the total into current, 1 to 30 days late and so on. The <strong>Activity Statement</strong> instead lists every invoice and payment between two dates.</p><div class="oe-callout"><span class="oe-callout-icon"><i class="fa fa-cog" /></span><div><span class="oe-callout-label">Switch them on first</span><p>Statements appear in the Actions menu once <strong>Outstanding Statement</strong> and <strong>Activity Statements</strong> are ticked in <span class="oe-path">Accounting › Configuration › Settings</span>, under Partner Statements.</p></div></div></div></field>
    </record>
    <record id="channel_books_s2" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_books" />
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="name">The bank</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
